    "lawCode": "Amd §2103, Ins L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7634A\n\nSPONSOR: MARCHIONE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the insurance law, in relation to\nlicensing requirements for insurance agents\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to expand the channels through which insur-\nance agents can qualify for licensure for property and casualty classes,\nespecially (but not limited to) by taking a course offered over the\ninternet.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subparagraph (B) of paragraph 2 of subsection (f) of 2\nsection 2103 of the insurance law to allow those seeking licensure as\ninsurance agents to participate in the equivalent of ninety classroom\nhours of training through correspondence work, a course offered over the\ninternet, or a similar institution.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder current statute, pre-licensing coursework for life insurance,\nannuity contracts, disability insurance, accident and health insurance\nand related insurances can be taken in either classroom format or equiv-\nalent correspondence / distance learning formats.  Personal Lines insur-\nance pre-licensing coursework may only be taken in classroom format.\nThis restriction presents a hardship for those in rural communities that\nare seeking to be licensed to sell Personal Lines insurance, because of\nthe distance they must travel and the cost of overnight accommodations\nduring the week-long course. This bill ensures greater access to pre-li-\ncensing coursework for all forms of insurance by creating the option for\nindividuals to take these courses over the internet or by other remote\nmethods.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
